      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/as-pure-r/q8-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"2𝑋+ 𝑌= 2 −22 −𝑌= −6𝑋 2𝑋−22 = 2 −6𝑋, 8𝑋= 24, 𝑋= 3. Substitute in 2𝑋+𝑌= 2. 6+𝑌= 2, so 𝑌= −4. Hence log2 𝑥= 3 gives 𝑥= 23 = 8 . Likewise log2 𝑦= −4 gives 𝑦= 2−4 = 1/16 .\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
